         "title": "Nuno Sousa: “I had one client that ate a francesinha like a sandwich, grabbing the ends of the bread. Beautiful memory”",
         "description": "<p><span>Chef Nuno Sousa left Barcelos for New York with no formal culinary training, a background in football coaching and a determination to build something of his own. Nearly a decade later, he runs Leitao, a Portuguese restaurant in Manhattan’s West Village that has become a reference point for Portuguese cuisine in the city. Listen to the premiere of The Heart and Hustle of Portugal’s Season 5, recorded on location in New York</span></p>",
